  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are RRR red gems and BBB blue gems. Each red gem can be sold for PPP coins, while a blue gem can be sold for QQQ coins.\n\nIt is not allowed to take gems of both colours. You may either take all of the red gems, or take all of the blue gems.\n\nFind the maximum number of coins you can obtain by taking some of the gems and then selling them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains 444 integers - R,B,P,QR, B, P, QR,B,P,Q.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum number of coins you can make.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤R,B,P,Q≤101 \\le R, B, P, Q \\le 101≤R,B,P,Q≤10."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 3 5 3",
        "output": "10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTaking the red gems would get you 2⋅5=102 \\cdot 5 = 102⋅5=10 coins, while taking the blue gems would get you 3⋅3=93 \\cdot 3 = 93⋅3=9 coins. Hence you should take the red gems."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 1 6 7",
        "output": "7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere is only 111 red gem and 111 blue gem. The blue gem sells for more, so you should take it, and get 777 coins."
      }
    ]
  },
